30,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It's worse than I thought. The wall is practically transparent to sound, and people are eating at their desks, leaving a mess everywhere.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,We've been spending a lot on outside rentals for small groups... and the fit-out quotes are quite different depending on the choice.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Rin,,"It's so unfair! Only two people use the room all the time, and one person always has to clean the fridge alone!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have lost our spaces for spontaneous connection. Even our difficult conversations are happening in public, which is quite sad.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The maintenance on this floor is uneven, and the time spent walking for lunch is a significant drain on our daily productivity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, if we're paying for outside rooms, why not just fix the one we have? But we must solve the noise issue first.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I just worry about who signs for the costs. The outside hire is a monthly drain we could stop if we had a proper space.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, does the lunch walk take a long time? Maybe that's why people are eating at their desks and making crumbs!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your observation is keen. If we lack a place to gather or speak privately, we become strangers in our own office.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, yes, it's nearly half an hour. The inefficiency is clear. We are wasting time and creating a mess because the room is misused.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Shion,,"If we make it a kitchen, the crumbs just move from the desks to the room, and the noise will still leak through that thin wall.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"A meeting space might be cheaper to fit out than a full kitchen, and it would stop those outside hire invoices.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if it's just for meetings, will it still be a place where we can just hang out? I don't want it to be boring!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Servas,,"A space for dialogue, whether formal or informal, would heal the rift between us. We need a sanctuary for honest communication.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"A kitchen requires constant upkeep. I've seen how ""shared"" cleaning usually falls on one person. A meeting space is more sustainable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I'm not interested in ""healing rifts,"" but I am interested in not hearing every word of a phone call from my desk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I agree with Toshio. A meeting space seems more fiscally responsible and solves the rental problem.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I just want it to be fair! No more ""first come, first served"" or one person cleaning everything!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us consider if a quiet room might serve us, or if the need for connection outweighs the need for silence.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Silence is a luxury, but efficiency is a necessity. Let's see the options.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
